.TH MCHECK 1
.SH NAME
mcheck \- independently verify a monoca epoch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcheck
.RI [ name pkhex exp ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcheck
re-reads
.BR /keydb/monoca/leaves ,
.BR /keydb/monoca/epoch ,
.BR /keydb/monoca/roots/\fIn\fP
and
.BR /keydb/mono-signer.pub ,
then reports:
.IP \(bu
whether the epoch record's signature verifies with any key in
.BR /keydb/mono-signer.pub ;
.IP \(bu
whether the root recomputed from the leaves equals the signed root;
.IP \(bu
whether every leaf's inclusion path verifies;
.IP \(bu
whether an unenrolled name can be proven absent;
.IP \(bu
whether the retained previous epoch verifies;
.IP \(bu
negative controls: a corrupted signature and a present leaf offered as
absent must both fail;
.IP \(bu
whether the epoch is fresh against the clock and its window.
.PP
With
.IR "name pkhex exp"
it also proves that leaf absent, which is how a revoked or rotated key
is checked.  Each line prints a value and the expected one, so the
output can be read without knowing the internals.
.PP
It shares only the Merkle module with
.IR monoca (8);
the parser and the byte layout are written out again on purpose, so
agreement between the two is evidence that the format is implemented
as documented.
.SH FILES
.TF /keydb/monoca/epoch
.TP
.B /keydb/monoca/leaves
authorised set
.TP
.B /keydb/monoca/epoch
current signed record
.TP
.B /keydb/monoca/roots/\fIn\fP
retained previous records
.TP
.B /keydb/mono-signer.pub
trusted EdDSA signer public keys
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/mcheck.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR monoca (8),
.IR mono (2),
.IR monosigner (2)
